Z||000000||BN Boomer||08-06-99||04:44 PM||||Thanks again for the engine and interior pieces.<p>I see in another thread that you are looking for some brackets to mount that Getrag transmission in your car. I recently saw a local add from somebody parting out an 86 GT with the 2.8 and I think a 5 speed tranny. I don't profess to know much about Fieros, so I was wondering if this car might have the brackets you need. Was the Getrag the only 5 speed used with V6 cars? If so, I can find out more. Let me know. 
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||08-06-99||06:46 PM||||Hello BN Boomer. <p>The Getrag is the only 5spd that came with the V6, but in 86 some of the GT's had 4 spds. There are 2 brackets I need. One is pretty big and it holds the shift cable and the slave cylinder. The other bracket I need is a smaller one mounted lower down and holds the selector cable. If these are available let me know. The Pontiac dealer said they were discontinued about 7 years ago and these are very hard to find in boneyards. If they are available I will send you the money to snag them and send them my way. Just for kicks, ask him what he would take for the whole tranny.<p>How is the motor going? Is it in yet? Do you need the wiring harness or anything else I forgot to give you?
Z||000002||BN Boomer||08-10-99||06:03 PM||||<b>UPDATE</b><p>Well, it turns out that the 86 GT being parted is an automatic. Sorry about that one...<p>I haven't been able to gt started on the motor swap. I've got a Honda Civic that received a recent transplant and I need to get that finished up before I can start on the Fiero. I tell ya, those damn rice burners are the absolute worst things to work on.
